README.source for the ssh3-go Debian package
============================================

What this package builds
-------------------------

Two binaries from one Go module tree (the nagual2 fork of
francoismichel/ssh3, module github.com/francoismichel/ssh3):

  * /usr/bin/ssh3         - the SSH3 client (cmd/ssh3)
  * /usr/bin/ssh3-server  - the SSH3 daemon (cmd/ssh3-server)

Both are Go PIE binaries linked through the gcc front end
(-buildmode=pie, CGO_ENABLED=1) so that the dpkg hardening ladder
(DEB_BUILD_MAINT_OPTIONS=hardening=+all: the stack protector,
fortify sources, RELRO, bind-now) applies to the C runtime pieces;
CGO is required by the crypt password backend of the amd64 build
(util/unix_util, libcrypt).

The Debian maintainer files live in the upstream tree under
packaging/debian/ and are copied to debian/ of the assembled source
tree before dpkg-buildpackage (see .github/workflows/debian-package.yml
for the exact sequence).

The vendor/ tree
----------------

The module ships its dependency tree vendored (go mod vendor), and
the orig tarball is a verbatim git archive of the upstream tag
including vendor/.  The build pins -mod=vendor and GOTOOLCHAIN=local:
no network access is needed after the orig is assembled, no
toolchain download can happen mid-build.

One deliberate irregularity: vendor/h3 is NOT a Go module - it is
the vendored h3 Rust crate of the [patch.crates-io] section in the
root Cargo.toml (the SSH3-Rust workspace lineage).  It is not part
of the Go build and not part of this package; go's vendor-mode
consistency check tolerates it (verified with Go 1.26).

Toolchain
---------

go.mod declares the Go floor 1.26; the package targets unstable,
where golang-any (2:1.27~1 at the time of writing) satisfies
Build-Depends: golang-any (>= 2:1.26~).  The trixie toolchain
(1.24) does NOT satisfy the floor - the package is an unstable
target, not a stable backport.

Drop-in replacement dance
-------------------------

The binary package ssh3-go ships the same /usr/bin/ssh3 and
/usr/bin/ssh3-server interfaces as the sibling C17 implementation
(source ssh3-c, binary package ssh3-server).  Both sides declare
Conflicts/Replaces against each other, so installing either one
replaces the other; the systemd unit, the conffile
/etc/ssh3/ssh3-server.env and the man pages follow the same paths in
both packages.

The Go daemon has no socket-activation support (no sd_listen_fds
handling): unlike ssh3-c, this package ships a plain service unit
binding UDP/443 itself; the enable/restart cycle is carried by
dh_installsystemd (policy 9.3), the maintainer scripts contain no
direct systemctl calls.

Tests
-----

The upstream ginkgo/pytest-style suite (integration_tests/) needs
generated SSH keys, test users and a running server; it runs in the
project CI (.github/workflows/test.yml), not in the packaging
build (debian/rules overrides dh_auto_test).  The packaging build
verifies the build itself: two binaries, PIE, against the vendored
tree.

Building
--------

  # from an assembled tree (orig + debian/ side by side)
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -S   # source
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b   # binary
  lintian --fail-on error ../ssh3-go_*.changes
